<li>When names are searched, they are matched with a wildcard at the end: thus, an employee entered as "Davis, Jean" would be matched by a "Davis, Jean Luc", or "Davis, Jean L.", but not by a "Davis, Jeannette".</li>
<li>You do not need to worry about capitalization or apostrophes. Hyphens can be entered ("Jean-Luc").</li>
<li>Because of the inconsistent nature of middle names in recordkeeping across the agencies we monitor, we do NOT search by middle name.</li>
<li>We strongly recommend entering a SSN and a DOB in order to avoid false positive potential matches.</li>
<li>If you enter a Louisiana license number, the Louisiana State Board of Medical Examiners website will be searched for license expirations.</li>
